            <p>
              Cats are <strong>obligate carnivores</strong>. Unlike dogs or humans who can synthesize key vitamins from plants, cats have an absolute biological requirement for animal meat tissue. Their diet must provide high levels of <strong>crude animal protein</strong>, fat, and two crucial non-negotiable amino acids: <strong>Taurine</strong> (which prevents fatal dilated cardiomyopathy and retinal blindness) and <strong>Arachidonic Acid</strong>.
            </p>
